AB  - Abdominal splenosis is found in posttraumatic patients where splenic tissue was spread in the abdominal cavity. While most of the cases are asymptomatic others can be present with abdominal pain, gastrointestinal bleeding, constipation, or an abdominal tumor mass which can mimic malignancy. We present a case of a 51 - years old female with multiple tumor masses in the abdominal cavity and symptoms of a small bowel obstruction. © 2021 Izdatelstvo Medicina i Fizkultura. All rights reserved.
