AB  - Torsion of the female abdominal and pelvic organs are rare but can lead to severe sequelae including life-threatening shock due to organ ischemia. The ovaries are most commonly affected, followed by the gallbladder and spleen. Clinically, organ torsion often presents as an acute abdomen. Sonography and computed tomography may show the so-called»whirlpool sign«, indicating acute torsion, particularly of the ovaries and spleen. Urgent surgery is required to save the patient, while also saving the organ itself. © 2024 Mediengruppe Oberfranken - Fachverlage GmbH & Co. KG. All rights reserved.
