AB  - Two years old castrated male Dachshund was brought to the hospital with history of frequent vomiting for the one week. Plain radiography revealed gas filled intestine where as delayed gastric emptying was observed in contrast study. Exploratory laparotomy was performed and the condition was diagnosed as gastric volvulus with splenic torsion and pyloric stenosis. Pyloric stenosis was corrected by pyloroplasty, gastric volvulus and splenic torsion were manually corrected and prophylactic incisional gastropexy was done to prevent recurrence.
