AB  - Wandering spleen is a very rare condition characterized by the absence or the weakness of one or more of the ligaments that keep the spleen in its normal position - in the upper left abdomen. As a result, the organ migrates from its usual anatomical position, usually to the lower abdomen or pelvis. X-ray evaluation includes ultrasound, Doppler, computed tomography (CT) or magnetic resonance imaging (MRI). We present a clinical case of a 74 years old woman who was admitted to the surgery department due to ileal symptoms, and the imaging examinations revealed a greatly enlarged and ectopically located spleen. Our report illustrates a rare clinical case that can present a challenging diagnosis.especially in the cases of clinical emergency. © 2021 Izdatelstvo Medicina i Fizkultura. All rights reserved.
