AB  - Splenic torsion is a surgical emergency encountered in deep chested large breeds of dogs (McNish et al., 1967 and Lipowitz et al., 1974). Etiology of the condition is not clear but its pathophysiologic consequences can be catastrophic. Number of clinical cases with attempts at treatment have been reported (Lipowitz et al., 1977 and Stead et al., 1983). The present study was undertaken to study the haematological changes following torsion of spleen.
