AB  - Torsion of spleen resulting in splenomegaly is being reported with increasing frequency in dogs. When combined with acute onset, clinical signs of vomiting, abdominal pain, progressive abdominal distension, depression, paleness of mucous membrane and palpable abdominal mass, should be sufficient to indicate torsion of the splenic pedicle. These signs constitute an emergency that must be managed rapidly.
