AB  - A case of wandering spleen in a 30-year-old male is presented which had evaded clinical diagnosis and was discovered on exploratory laparotomy. A huge spleen with definite notch was found in the pelvis. It had an elongated pedicle extending into the left hypochondrium. Splenectomy was done. Follow-up at 2 and 10 months indicated that the patient was asymptomatic with complete resolution of symptoms.
