AD  - Klinika Detske Chir. 2. LF UK, FN V Motole, 150 18 Praha 5 - Motol, V Úvalu 84, Czech Republic
AB  - The authors describe two cases of torsion of the spleen in children aged 4 and 7 and a half years, treated at the Clinic of Paediatric Surgery, Faculty Hospital Motol in 1994 and 1995 (after a nine-month interval). A period of 40 years separates these two cases from a previous one which was treated at the Clinic on account of this diagnosis. Splenectomy was the solution in all children because of ischaemia of the spleen. The preoperative diagnoses differed, however, not only due to the clinical examination but also because of different technical diagnostic facilities. Based on a review of the literature the authors discuss the epidemiology, etiology, pathophysiology, diagnosis and therapy of this disease.
