AB  - Objective: To seek CT and angiographic appearances that characterize torsion of the wandering spleen.  Materials and Methods: The CT and angiographic findings of two cases of preoperatively diagnosed torsion of the wandering spleen were reviewed, and the findings were closely compared with intraoperative and histopathological findings. Results: Characteristic CT appearance seemed to be a whirled appearance formed at the medial side of the displaced spleen. The angiographic finding that was characteristic of the disease was a tapered and abruptly twisted distal splenic artery. Conclusion: These findings were useful in making the early and correct diagnosis of this rare but fulminant condition. © 1995 Raven Press, Ltd., New York.
