AB  - The diagnosis of wandering spleen by sulfur colloid imaging has previously been established by scan visualization of the spleen in an unusual location. These reports, however, have not actually demonstrates splenic movement during the examination, and occasionally have required serial studies following vigorous exercise. A case is presented in which anterior decubitus views documented splenic wandering due to laxity of the supporting ligaments.
