AB  - The wandering spleen is a rare disease in childhood and is accompanied by a congenital or acquired dislocation of the spleen, which may be presented as an abdominal tumor mass. In cases of torsion of the vascular supply thrombosis or necrosis of the whole organ produces clinical signs of an ‘acute abdomen’. A diagnosis is easy to make with sonographic findings. An immediate operation is necessary to preserve the organ. A new operative procedure making it possible to preserve the spleen is de-scribed. © 1993 S. Karger AG, Basel.
